Production Handling Unit
########################

Adds the handling unit concept to production cycles and work center-product
assignments.

Handling unit requests
======================

Configure the container type, entry behaviour, required number, measurement
unit and missing-unit entry on the routing operation, once per company.
New routing steps inherit this configuration. A step can instead request a
container, retrieve a previous container or disable container entry.

Step exceptions can select several products or categories. Categories include
their descendants. Product exceptions take precedence over category exceptions,
then the step setting takes precedence over the operation setting. Conflicting
exceptions at the same priority are rejected.

The operation's source operations define where to retrieve previous containers.
In Valero, selecting a previous cycle retains its container type and number.
The measurement unit defaults to the production unit; product assignments are
not required for new cycles.

Upgrades preserve existing step settings as explicit overrides. Select
"Inherit from Operation" on those steps to use a common configuration.
Cycles retain a snapshot of their handling-unit settings, so subsequent changes
to the operation or exceptions do not alter existing cycles.
